  <challenge>
    <id>20</id>
    <title>Ascertain Most Frequent Character</title>
    <description>Given a string, `TEXT`, return the character that appears most frequently (excluding
      spaces). Assume a tie cannot exist. Assume a
      predefined ordered array `LETTERS` contains all 26 lowercase letters (index 0 to 25) of
      the alphabet in order.</description>
    <hint>The "length" property may be used on a string. Create a 26-long array initialized to zero by invoking the Array method `set_length(26,0)`
      method to be able to count how many times each letter in
      the alphabet appears. Use the
      index from `LETTERS` to match characters and store their frequencies.</hint>
    <tags>
      <tag>Strings</tag>
      <tag>Loops</tag>
      <tag>Arrays</tag>
    </tags>
    <dataTypes>
      <inputType>String of characters.</inputType>
      <inputName>TEXT</inputName>
      <inputType>Ordered (A-Z) array that contains all lowercase letters (index 0 to 25).</inputType>
      <inputName>LETTERS</inputName>
      <outputType>String that is single character representing the most frequent character.</outputType>
    </dataTypes>
    <difficulty>SL</difficulty>
    <testCases>
      <testCase>
        <input>CustomString("banana")</input>
        <input>
          Array("a","b","c","d","e","f","g","h","i","j","k","l","m","n","o","p","q","r","s","t","u","v","w","x","y","z")</input>
        <output>a</output>
      </testCase>
      <testCase>
        <input>CustomString("hello")</input>
        <input>
          Array("a","b","c","d","e","f","g","h","i","j","k","l","m","n","o","p","q","r","s","t","u","v","w","x","y","z")</input>
        <output>l</output>
      </testCase>
      <testCase>
        <input>CustomString("cool")</input>
        <input>
          Array("a","b","c","d","e","f","g","h","i","j","k","l","m","n","o","p","q","r","s","t","u","v","w","x","y","z")</input>
        <output>o</output>
      </testCase>
    </testCases>
  </challenge>

</challenges>